  "text": "David swore to kill every male in that household. The Bible's exact words are \"any that pisseth against the wall.\" Nabal. Three thousand sheep. Shearing season. He is throwing a feast \"like the feast of a king.\" David's men had guarded his shepherds for free. His own staff say it: they were a wall unto us, night and day. David sends ten men. Asks for food. And Nabal says, \"Who is David? and who is the son of Jesse?\" Sir. David's answer: \"Gird ye on every man his sword.\" Four hundred men. Over dinner. A servant runs to the wife. Nobody can talk to Nabal. Abigail does not panic. She does inventory. Two hundred loaves. Two bottles of wine. Five dressed sheep. Roasted corn. A hundred clusters of raisins. Two hundred cakes of figs. On donkeys. Sent ahead. \"But she told not her husband Nabal.\" Then she rides at four hundred swords and calls her own husband a fool to his face. \"Nabal is his name, and folly is with him.\" She talks him down. Four hundred men turn around. He is drunk when she gets home, so she waits till morning. \"His heart died within him, and he became as a stone.\" Ten days later he is dead. And David, the man riding out to kill him, sends for her. She married him.",
